			"Message": "docs(Vine): Streamline README with concise benefit-focused content\n\nRestructure the Vine README from a verbose 200+ line document to a ~100 line concise format. Key changes include:\n\n- Shorten and rewrite content in benefit-focused language matching the website's outcome-oriented direction\n- Add a punchy problem/solution opening (\"Electron's IPC is untyped...\") followed by the value proposition\n- Update Rust icon to use editor.land CDN instead of simpleicons.org\n- Remove detailed architecture tables, planned features lists, and system diagram sections\n- Consolidate sections into focused areas: What It Does, In the Ecosystem, Development, License\n- Add new documentation links (Vine Documentation, Why gRPC)\n\nThe README now leads with the core value proposition and is easier to scan, aligning with the marketing website's goal-oriented copy style.",
